.find = first occurence of what in the ""
.rfind() = last occurrence of whats in the ""
.capitalize() = capitalize first letter
.upper() = upper case full string
.lower() = lower case full string
.isdigit() = returns true if string only contains digits
.isalpha() = returns true if string only contains characters
.count("x") = returns number of x characters inside a string
.replace("x", "y") = replace x with y

Example:
user_name = input("Enter a user name: ")

if len(user_name) > 12:
    print("User name cant be more than 12 characters")
elif not user_name.find(" ") == -1:
    print("User name cant contain spaces")
elif not user_name.isalpha():
    print("User cant contain digits")
else:
    print(f"Welcome {user_name}")
